Interview questions [1]

Question 1

Eqvilent hiring process 1h30 online quiz: mostly code snippets that I had to guess the output of (website wont let you copy text to compile & run obviously). Advanced questions on NRVO and RVO (see CppCon video on this subject) std::discrete_distribution to generate numbers. Code showing SPSC queue; find the bug. for loop looping doing std::numeric_limits::max() iterations, cout <<”i” at each iteration. Q: What time does it take to complete all iterations? Q: Implement int isGreater(int a, int b) without branches (should return 1, 0 or -1). Use branchless programming. Q: Not a coding question but calculate the price of a product after two discounts (percentages). Home Assignment (should be completed within 7 days) Implement a program to parse pcap files containing Simba messages (Simba is a market exchange protocol, look up latest version on web). The messages should be decoded and exported to Json. OrderExec, OrderUpdate and OrderSnapshot are the only messages that you need to implement. Be careful of big endian-little endian and packing of structures. 1h tech itw Q: If std::vector reallocates, are the contents moved or copied? A: If move constructor is noexcept they are moved. Otherwise they are copied (This prevents having an exception after having moved several elements which are therefore irreversibly modified). Q: Why is std::function bad for performance? A: 1)Type erasure (virtual call is made) is used by this class 2) it may also allocate on the heap (thus inducing a cache miss) Q: What are the avg time complexities of vector reallocation, std::map operations? Diff between layout in memory of map and unordered_map. When does a rehashing happen in unordered_map? A: See load_factor and bucket capacity. Then go on Leetcode and solve a multithreading problem: Use condition_variables to ensure synchronization of threads. You start to code until the interviewer sees you have found the correct solution. Then look at a simple code with several shared_ptrs which have circular dependencies. Q: What is the problem here? A: There is a cycle between shared_ptrs, therefore memory won’t be released correctly. Q: Have you used CPU isolation in your previous work? Thread pinning? Q: Difference between poll and select for Unix sockets. 1h technical itw Leecode style problems Q: Implement function that takes an array of integers as input. Output an array with the same integers but all the zeros should be at the end. The relative order of the integers should be preserved and you have to modify the input array in-place. A: Use two pointers and std::swap Q: Implement function that takes an array of ints. Output array of strings with consecutive numbers as such input [1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 9] output [“1-3”, ”5-6”, “9”] A: Use std::deque Make sure to think thoroughly before typing, because you cannot run your code, the interviewer will confirm when its ok.
